    "bio": "A Representative from Michigan; born in Livingston County, Mich., June 2, 1963; graduated from Howell High School, Howell, Mich., 1981; B.S., Adrian College, Adrian, Mich., 1985; United States Army, 1985-1989; Federal Bureau of Investigation, 1989-1994; member of the Michigan state senate, 1995-2000, and majority floor leader, 1999-2000; elected as a Republican to the One Hundred Seventh and to the six succeeding Congresses (January 3, 2001-January 3, 2015); was not a candidate for reelection to the One Hundred Fourteenth Congress in 2014; chair, Permanent Select Committee on Intelligence (One Hundred Twelfth and One Hundred Thirteenth Congresses); was an unsuccessful candidate for the United States Senate in 2024.",
